  "generated_text": "1. Let \\( x = 0.\\overline{42} \\).\n2. Multiply both sides by 100 to shift the decimal point:\n   \\[\n   100x = 42.\\overline{42}\n   \\]\n3. Subtract the original \\( x \\) from this new equation:\n   \\[\n   100x - x = 42.\\overline{42} - 0.\\overline{42}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   99x = 42\n   \\]\n4. Solve for \\( x \\):\n   \\[\n   x = \\frac{42}{99}\n   \\]\n5. Simplify the fraction \\(\\frac{42}{99}\\):\n   \\[\n   \\frac{42}{99} = \\frac{4}{11}\n   \\]\n6. Therefore, \\( a = 4 \\) and \\( b = 11 \\).\n7. Calculate \\( a + b \\):\n   \\[\n   a + b = 4 + 11 = 15\n   \\boxed{15}",
  "grade": {
